      "content": "1. Muscular and Skeletal System – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The human skeletal system provides structural framework, protects internal organs, and facilitates locomotion.",
        "Joints connect bones and are categorized into fibrous, cartilaginous, and synovial types based on degree of mobility.",
        "Ligaments attach bone to bone, while tendons connect muscle to bone.",
        "Muscular tissues are classified into three major types: skeletal (striated/voluntary), smooth (visceral/involuntary), and cardiac muscles.",
        "Common muscular and skeletal disorders include Osteoporosis, Arthritis, Tetany, and Myasthenia Gravis."
      ],
      "id": "yobieod"
